WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.880
At long last, filmmaker M. Night Shyamalan
has completed a trilogy of movies that he

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.500
secretly started back in the year 2000 with
Unbreakable.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.180
True to form as ever, he left plenty of twists
in store for the final act.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.129
It was almost too much to keep track of, so
let's break down what happened during the

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:17.480
ending of Glass.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:23.320
Unbreakable introduced viewers to Elijah Price,
a.k.a. Mr. Glass, a mysterious, intense, and

00:00:23.339 --> 00:00:25.699
seemingly unbalanced comic book dealer.

00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:30.399
After discovering security guard David Dunn
to be the sole survivor of a devastating trainwreck,

00:00:30.399 --> 00:00:34.390
Price spends the movie encouraging him to
embrace the idea that he's been gifted with

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.900
superhuman abilities.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.250
In the grounded world of the movie, it comes
off as a wacky idea.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.460
But Elijah is ultimately proven right; David
slowly comes to realize he's nearly invulnerable,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.760
can see into people's thoughts by touching
them, and possesses incredible strength.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.621
Reluctantly, he begins putting his powers
to use in an effort to bring evildoers to

00:00:52.621 --> 00:00:55.590
justice - a security guard on a grand scale.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.570
Of course, this being an M. Night Shyamalan
picture, there's more to the story than initially

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:05.109
meets the eye: Elijah's motives for awakening
David to his powers are far from altruistic.

00:01:05.109 --> 00:01:09.340
It's revealed that he actually orchestrated
the deadly events that led to his discovery

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.569
of David in the first place, causing many
other incidents of domestic terror before

00:01:13.569 --> 00:01:16.799
sabotaging the Eastrail 177 train.

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:20.000
Elijah sees himself as the perfect foil to
Dunn's superhero.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.200
There's plenty of symmetry backing up Elijah's
point of view, right down to the rare bone

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:28.170
disease that renders him just as physically
fragile as David is strong.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:32.030
But David refuses to play by the rules of
his would-be arch-nemesis.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.539
As Unbreakable ends, we learn that Elijah
has been arrested and committed to an institution

00:01:36.539 --> 00:01:37.749
for the criminally insane.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:40.560
And that was the end of the story - until
Split.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.560
David refuses to be drawn into a super-rivalry
with Elijah, but that doesn't mean he rejects

00:01:45.569 --> 00:01:47.509
the potential of his powers outright.

00:01:47.509 --> 00:01:52.200
As we learn about in Glass, David adopts the
alter ego of the Overseer, dedicating himself

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.590
to ferreting out evil with the assistance
of his son Joseph.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.360
It would have been interesting to learn more
about David's exploits in the time between

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:04.090
Unbreakable and Split, since fans of the first
movie had spent years wondering if a more

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.450
traditional sequel could be on the way.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.810
Instead, audiences are reintroduced to David
at a pivotal moment, as he learns about the

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:16.000
existence of Kevin Wendell Crumb, a.k.a. the
Horde, whose psychotic exploits become public

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.790
during Split's closing minutes.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:22.060
When Glass begins, we see David trying to
track down Kevin in an effort to foil his

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.000
latest kidnapping - and he does a pretty good
job.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.780
After bumping into Kevin on the street and
learning his dark secret, he heads straight

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.180
for Kevin's hideout, frees his victims, and
then faces off against his adversary.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:37.041
Their showdown is cut short by the arrival
of well-prepared law enforcement, who show

00:02:37.041 --> 00:02:40.590
up determined to take both men into custody
- not just Kevin.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:44.620
Without so much as a court hearing, the duelling
superhumans are locked up inside a mental

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.760
institution - one that has also spent years
housing Elijah Price.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:54.600
With David and Kevin at the institution, Elijah
has all the pieces in place to execute a masterwork

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:55.780
of supervillainy.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:03:00.370
With the Overseer, Elijah has his perfect
adversary; in the Horde, he has a useful ally.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:05.510
Several of them, actually - Kevin lives with
24 distinct personalities, including the supernatural

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.090
one called "The Beast."

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:11.280
This personality is imbued with incredible
strength, the ability to climb walls, and

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.980
a desire to rid the world of "impure" individuals
who've never known suffering.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:19.980
Elijah is physically weak but intellectually
brilliant, while Kevin is incredibly strong

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:21.700
but psychologically unstable.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:25.950
Together, they team up to execute an escape
plan, teasing the audience with a climactic

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.670
showdown in the heart of Philadelphia.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:31.870
But what Elijah says he wants to do is not
what he's actually going to do.

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:36.130
As they make their way out of the psychiatric
facility, only Mr. Glass knows the full shape

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.360
of what's really going on.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.220
"That sounds like the bad guys teaming up."

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.220
The showdown

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.150
Elijah's plan is to expose the existence of
superheroes to the world on a grand scale,

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:49.710
letting people know beyond a shadow of a doubt
that humans are capable of extraordinary things,

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.640
just like in the comic books he loves so much.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:55.990
At first, he claims his plan is to have the
Horde and the Overseer go toe-to-toe with

00:03:55.990 --> 00:04:00.770
each other at the high-profile opening of
a new skyscraper in downtown Philadelphia.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:05.040
But once he escapes the facility with Kevin,
they never get further than the parking lot.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:09.970
Neither David, Kevin, nor Elijah make any
effort to get to the tower for their showdown,

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.930
instead having their fight on the hospital
grounds.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:15.740
To the audience, it seems like Elijah's plan
is going off the rails, and that he's going

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:20.090
to be prevented from completing his mission
of waking people up to the existence of superheroes.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:24.480
By the end of the movie, we learn that everything
is actually going according to plan.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:28.520
In the hospital parking lot, The Overseer
and the Horde duke it out with each other

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:33.160
while Mr. Glass watches and provides commentary,
almost like the whole battle is a movie he's

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.160
directing.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.870
All the while, Dr. Ellie Staple is frantically
attempting to bring reinforcements of some

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:41.440
kind to the facility in order to bring the
situation under control.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.180
When they arrive, one of the most shocking
moments in the movie happens - and we're not

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:50.281
talking about the reveal that Elijah's derailment
of Eastrail 177 also killed Kevin's dad.

00:04:50.281 --> 00:04:55.400
That twist, implying that Mr. Glass essentially
created the Horde, is relatively tame compared

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.570
to what happens next.

00:04:56.570 --> 00:05:00.820
When Staple's armed reinforcements show up,
they're once again suspiciously prepared for

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.270
the spectacle at hand.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:06.210
Instead of trying to de-escalate the situation
peacefully, they instead start trying to kill

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:09.750
the superhumans, exploiting their weaknesses
to catch them off guard.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:14.070
Dr. Staple enlists Casey to lure the Horde
away from the Beast persona, and back to his

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.960
baseline identity of Kevin Wendell Crumb.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:20.780
Once he's got the body of a normal human being
again, he's fatally shot by Staple's backup.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:23.310
He's not the only one to get such merciless
treatment.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:27.560
After fighting with Kevin in a tank of water,
David's strength is severely compromised.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.900
He's thrown off by being submerged in the
source of his one weakness, and when Dr. Staple's

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:36.420
backup approaches him, dressed like SWAT team
members, he's powerless to fight back.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:40.110
Instead of helping him or trying to take him
in peacefully, the men take a hold of David,

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.290
and drown him to death in a puddle of water.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:46.480
It's a devastating moment for viewers who
went in expecting a more traditional ending

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.480
to the story.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.120
As we all should have probably expected, Shyamalan
has no interest in giving people what they

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.200
expect.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.240
"No."

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:58.120
Before David dies at the hands of her backup,
Dr. Staple decides to explain to him just

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.180
what's really been going on at the facility.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:04.160
Essentially, she's been gaslighting all three
of them, attempting to make them believe that

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.230
their superpowers are only a delusion.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:09.850
She wasn't trying to help any of the superhumans
- she was trying to stop them.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:13.200
"So you're not going to shake my hand?”

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:17.370
After taking Dr. Staples' hand, David sees
in his final vision that she is a part of

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:21.669
an elaborate secret society - one that has
spent a very long time trying to prevent real

00:06:21.669 --> 00:06:24.970
superheroes from gaining a foothold in the
wider consciousness.

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:30.370
Dr. Staple's job is to go from city to city,
hunting down isolated incidents of superheroism

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:33.010
and shutting them down before they get too
much attention.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:37.890
She says she prefers to do this in a nonlethal
way, convincing people to give up their so-called

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.230
delusions so that she can spare their lives.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:43.010
If they don't, well - she lets her teammates
kill them.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:46.870
She also lets Elijah die from injuries he
suffered when the Beast turned his awesome

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:50.540
strength on him, after it was revealed that
he was responsible for the death of Kevin's

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:51.540
father.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:55.330
Once the three superhumans are dead, the members
of the mysterious society - who all share

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:59.610
the same tattoo of a clover on the wrist - set
about erasing all the evidence that indicates

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.320
a fight between superhumans even happened.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:06.669
Dr. Staple previously told Elijah that more
than a hundred cameras were recording activity

00:07:06.669 --> 00:07:11.240
on the facility's grounds, and her group goes
about the process of erasing all of that footage.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:15.580
They advise regular staff members of the hospital
to keep the incident to themselves, and almost

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:19.290
look like they're going to successfully sweep
everything under the rug, like they've apparently

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.960
done so many times before.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.580
But again, that's not what actually happens.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:26.820
Turns out, nothing that Dr. Staple can do
is capable of stopping Mr. Glass’s true

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:27.720
plan.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:32.199
Unbeknownst to Dr. Staple, the Overseer, or
the Horde, Mr. Glass made arrangements to

00:07:32.199 --> 00:07:36.590
record all of the surveillance cameras at
some offsite location, broadcasting the footage

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:38.750
elsewhere so that it couldn't be erased.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:43.850
This cache of valuable video is then sent
to Joseph, Casey, and Mrs. Price, all of whom

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:46.340
were there to see the fantastic events as
they unfolded.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:50.690
Thanks to Elijah's data drop, the three survivors
have more than just their eyewitness testimony

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:55.370
- they have footage of superhuman feats, recorded
by dozens of cameras, which they can now blast

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:59.759
out into the world, defeating the scheme of
Dr. Staple's secret society.

00:07:59.759 --> 00:08:03.620
After the superhumans are dead, these three
regular strangers work together to share the

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:07.650
footage with the world, uploading it to the
internet - and then they sit and wait as people

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:10.080
around them begin to hear the incredible news.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.770
All around them, people see with their own
eyes what seems to be proof of the existence

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:14.880
of superheroes.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:19.520
The secret society's mission has been foiled
- Mr. Glass' plan was a success.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:24.000
The biggest twist in Glass, aside from the
reveals of the Horde's real origin story,

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.720
Mr. Glass' real plan, and the unexpected deaths
of the main characters, is arguably the existence

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:30.300
of the secret society.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:34.229
It's clear from the glimpses we get that the
group possesses significant resources to help

00:08:34.229 --> 00:08:35.290
them execute their mission.

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:39.680
But the film gives us very little insight
into what the organization actually is, or

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:43.589
what it might do now that the cat's out of
the bag regarding the whole superhero thing.

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:47.580
They apparently want to maintain balance in
the world - but now that balance is tipping.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:52.040
Not only does the archive of security camera
footage show real superheroes in action, it

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:56.980
also shows proof of Dr. Staple's organization
blatantly executing David and Kevin, both

00:08:56.980 --> 00:09:00.060
of whom are basically defenseless at the time
they're killed.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.770
David's death is particularly merciless, and
now it's on tape for the world to see.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.950
Will there be repercussions?

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:06.760
Is their mission effectively over?

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:11.890
The ending doesn't tell us, but from Dr. Staple's
bloodcurdling scream after she realizes what's

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:14.440
happened, the outlook for her group doesn't
look too good.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:19.360
As the footage makes it way into the world,
Mrs. Price once again channels her son's obsession

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:22.490
with comics, declaring it to be the "beginning
of a universe."

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:26.810
She believes wholeheartedly that Elijah was
right, and that the reveal of real superheroes

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:31.390
will only inspire more extraordinary people
to step out of the shadows, recognize their

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:32.860
powers, and change the world.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:36.700
It's the sort of setup that cries out for
a sequel - so of course Shyamalan has said

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:37.700
he's not doing one.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:41.520
Speaking in an interview with Vulture in the
days leading up to Glass' release, the filmmaker

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:45.070
shut down all speculation about a sequel movie,
saying simply,

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:46.600
"Yeah, we’re not doing that though.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:50.450
[...] I have the sequel rights to most of
my movies, essentially for the reason to not

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:51.450
do them."

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:54.860
If he's telling the truth about that, then
it seems that Glass' hopeful ending is meant

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:58.770
to be a tease for your imagination only, rather
than a promise about what's to come.

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:02.940
In keeping with the trilogy's second installment,
people have been very split on their reactions

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:04.190
to the final movie.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:07.710
Whether you love it or hate it, you almost
have to admire Glass for doing pretty much

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:12.680
exactly the opposite of what audiences expected,
and still somehow leaving you wanting more.

